---
title: 'EpsilonDelta Inc. Privacy Policy'
effectiveDate: 'Effective Date: September 4, 2026'
---

EpsilonDelta Inc. (the "Company") complies with the Personal Information Protection Act and other applicable laws. This Privacy Policy explains how the Company protects personal information and handles related requests and concerns.

**Article 1 (Scope)**

This Privacy Policy applies to the Company's corporate website (epsilondelta.ai). If the Company offers a separate product or service in the future, it may publish a separate privacy policy reflecting the personal information processing activities of that product or service.

**Article 2 (Personal Information Processed, Purposes, and Retention Periods)**

The Company does not currently offer account registration, payment, or product service features through this website. However, when an individual contacts the Company by email, the Company may process the following information.

<dl class="policy-data-card">
  <div class="policy-data-field">
    <dt>Category</dt>
    <dd>Email inquiries</dd>
  </div>
  <div class="policy-data-field">
    <dt>Information Processed</dt>
    <dd>Email address, inquiry details, and information voluntarily provided in the inquiry, such as name, organization, or phone number</dd>
  </div>
  <div class="policy-data-field">
    <dt>Purpose</dt>
    <dd>Reviewing and responding to inquiries and related follow-up communication</dd>
  </div>
  <div class="policy-data-field">
    <dt>Retention Period</dt>
    <dd>Retained for three years from the date the inquiry is resolved, then deleted</dd>
  </div>
</dl>

Individuals may decline to provide personal information. However, the Company may be unable to respond if information necessary to handle the inquiry is not provided.

**Article 3 (Provision of Personal Information to Third Parties)**

The Company does not provide personal information to third parties unless the individual has separately consented or applicable law specifically requires or permits the provision.

**Article 4 (Outsourcing and Cross-Border Transfers)**

The Company does not currently outsource the processing of personal information collected through this website or transfer such information outside Korea. If outsourcing or a cross-border transfer occurs in the future, the Company will disclose the information required by applicable law in this Privacy Policy.

**Article 5 (Destruction of Personal Information)**

The Company destroys personal information without delay when the retention period expires or the purpose of processing has been achieved. Electronic files are securely deleted to prevent recovery or reproduction, and paper documents are shredded or incinerated. If applicable law requires continued retention, the information is stored separately from other personal information.

**Article 6 (Rights of Individuals and How to Exercise Them)**

Individuals may request access to, correction or deletion of, suspension of processing of, or withdrawal of consent regarding their personal information. Requests may be submitted by email to contact@epsilondelta.ai. After confirming the identity of the individual or authorized representative, the Company will respond without delay in accordance with applicable law. A request may be restricted or denied where permitted by law, in which case the Company will explain the reason.

**Article 7 (Automatically Generated Information and Cookies)**

When an individual visits the website, access records such as IP address, access date and time, browser type, and operating system information may be generated automatically to provide and secure the website. These records are used only for security and incident response, retained for up to three months, and then deleted.

The Company does not currently use cookies or online behavioral tracking tools to identify visitors or provide personalized advertising.

**Article 8 (Security Measures)**

The Company restricts access to personal information to authorized personnel and implements appropriate administrative and technical safeguards, including transmission protection and access controls.

**Article 9 (Chief Privacy Officer)**

*   **Name**: 윤성국
